{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790342643,"nonce":"jhiqGUrRgZloYpPA79l6MG2Xsg0=","title":"@kernel reduce returns the last yield instead of reducing","message":"compute() lowering with a direct `yield` in the body (crates/compiler/src/ssa.rs, has_direct_yield and the `yields.last()` result) evaluates the args, runs the body and returns the last yielded value. There is no accumulator and no reduction operator. A `yield` inside a `for` loop, the documented form (`for i in 0..len: yield data[i]`), is not a direct yield and falls through to the undefined `$Zyntax$compute` dispatch.\n\nThe grammar's `@kernel \u003cidentifier\u003e` directive has no slot for the operator either, so `reduce(+)`, `reduce(max)` and `reduce(+, axis=1)` cannot be written.\n\nWanted: a reduce that accumulates with a stated operator, lowered to vector partial accumulators plus a horizontal reduce, with value-checked tests on Cranelift, LLVM, wasm and the interpreter.","files":null}]}